-- mu-rec-guard-order: the order proof of gate SI-G6 and brief 3.11.
-- The body of "grow" is one elimination of its argument at the fibered
-- form of M1 Stage H, with a motive and a constructor address at every
-- branch, so the translation of lib/order.ml builds an elimination that
-- the checker accepts:  the twin of this body with the self call
-- replaced by a postulate of the same type checks and gives no error.
-- The certificate is refused all the same, because the argument of the
-- call is "succ m", which is an application and never guards a call
-- (ruling R1, SI-D5, kan-lang-tot-pin/lib/totality.ml:102-109).
--
-- The guard therefore runs first and the file is refused with the
-- termination line of SI-D6, which the sidecar pins.  A build that
-- translated first would build the well typed elimination, accept the
-- file and print no line at all, so this sidecar reads the order of the
-- two steps and not the refusal alone.  This is the file mutation SI-M1
-- kills.

mu N : Type 0 with
| zero : N
| succ : N -> N

def rec grow : N -> N := fun (n : N) => case n as x in N return N with | zero => zero | succ m => grow (succ m)
